# Frontier review and the next Reiyah experiment

Document ID: `reiyah.frontier-review`. Version: `0.1.0`.
12 October 2026. Exploratory literature review and proposed research direction.

**Continue bounded science; strengthen the comparator before expanding the
engine.** The most consequential new lead is a September paper on exact model
choice from partial labels. It overlaps the mathematics that a weak comparison
could otherwise misrepresent as Reiyah's advantage. The reviewed autonomy
systems supply useful methods and prospective evidence sources, but none of the
inspected releases supplies a complete new workflow comparison.

This review follows current primary documentation and then research methods,
proofs and limitations. It is targeted, not exhaustive. No driving stack, paper
benchmark or theorem was independently reproduced. Exact versions, capture
digests, access terms and private custody are recorded in the
[source ledger](../../evidence/frontier-review-2026-10-12.json). No third-party
paper, code or dataset payload is added to public Git history.

